# Never access env files

Do not read, search, open, copy, or parse env files. This includes shell commands, search tools, and scripts that load them.

Covered files:

- `.env`
- `.env.*` (`.env.local`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, `.env.example`, and the same names in any directory)
- Other dotenv files that hold connection strings or secrets

Do not quote their values in commands, replies, logs, or other files. Do not reconstruct a connection string from them.

If a task needs a variable, ask the user for the value or tell them which variable name to set. Use `.env.example` only when the user explicitly asks to edit that example file.
